#, no-c-format
msgid "The skinSpritesData tag"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tag has a special organization: each type of sprite (flag, infantry, "
"cavalry, cannon, firing cannon and exploding cannon) is defined by some "
"intItem and strItem and there is two more intItem giving positioning hints "
"for animations. The table below shows all the elements of the "
"skinSpritesData tag with some explanations. Only some sprites have a width "
"data. These are used for relative positioning during animations: the "
"cannons, firing or explosing should not \"move\" around the country's flag "
"during fight."
